        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a78d6028-cc0a-5ff8-8763-4b8458bdf4cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Appointment in Tokyo, USS Missouri (BB-63)\n- Organizations: Army Pictorial Service, Signal Corps, Army Air Forces, United States Navy, Warner Bros., War Activities Committee\n- People: General Douglas MacArthur\n- Events: surrender of Japan, signing of the instrument of surrender, end of World War II\n- Places: Philippines\n\nFacts:\n- In early 1942, General Douglas MacArthur and his men went into exile from the Philippines.\n- Appointment in Tokyo mainly follows General Douglas MacArthur and his men from their exile from the Philippines in early 1942 through the signing of the instrument of surrender on the USS Missouri on September 1, 1945.\n- Appointment in Tokyo is a 1945 documentary produced by the Army Pictorial Service, Signal Corps, with the cooperation of the Army Air Forces and the United States Navy.\n- Appointment in Tokyo was released by Warner Bros. for the War Activities Committee shortly after the surrender of Japan.\n- The USS Missouri was the site of the surrender of the Empire of Japan, which ended World War II.\n- The USS Missouri was the last battleship commissioned by the United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
